# Fix ReferenceError in Layout.tsx

The console log indicates an `Uncaught ReferenceError: isActive is not defined` at `Layout.tsx:95:58`. Analysis reveals that `isActive` is being accessed outside the scope where it is defined by `react-router-dom`'s `NavLink`.

## Proposed Changes

### [Layout Component](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/components/Layout.tsx)

#### [MODIFY] [Layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/components/Layout.tsx)

- Update [NavItem](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/components/Layout.tsx#6-30) to properly access `isActive` by using the function-as-a-child pattern for `NavLink`.
- Update the mobile navigation loop to properly access `isActive` using the function-as-a-child pattern for `NavLink`.

```diff
-            <Icon size={18} strokeWidth={isActive ? 2.5 : 2} className="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-110" />
-            <span className="font-semibold text-sm tracking-tight">{label}</span>
-            <NavLink to={to}>
-                {({ isActive }) => isActive && (
-                    <motion.div
-                        layoutId="nav-dot"
-                        className="ml-auto w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-indigo-400"
-                    />
-                )}
-            </NavLink>
+            {({ isActive }) => (
+                <>
+                    <Icon size={18} strokeWidth={isActive ? 2.5 : 2} className="transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-110" />
+                    <span className="font-semibold text-sm tracking-tight">{label}</span>
+                    {isActive && (
+                        <motion.div
+                            layoutId="nav-dot"
+                            className="ml-auto w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-indigo-400"
+                        />
+                    )}
+                </>
+            )}
```

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None, as this is a UI-only fix.

### Manual Verification
1. Run the app using `npm run dev`.
2. Open the browser and check the console.
3. Verify that the `ReferenceError` is gone.
4. Navigate through the sidebar and mobile bottom bar to ensure active states are correctly highlighted with the dot and stroke width change.
